{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Software Architecture"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about software architecture."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Interpret the technical design report, to determine the work plan during the phase of building the software, based on regulation and protocols established by the company.   Design the architecture design using the appropriate tools and types according to the software requirements."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.   Recognizes simple ideas on persisting storage, web applications, and the functional phase of an IT project."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adverbs of Manner"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <strong>adverbs</strong> of manner to say how we do something."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>Adverbs of manner</strong> show how things happen and answer the question (how). Adverbs of manner go in end position or after the verb if there is no object. Let&rsquo;s see some adverbs of manner:</p> <p><i>Angrily, happily, fast, slowly, well, wrong, hard, carefully</i></p> <p>If the adverb ends in <strong>&ndash;ly</strong>, they can go in mid position before the verb when the adverb is not the focus of the idea.</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>Children <strong>easily</strong> understand the app.</i></p> <p><i>You must code it <strong>carefully</strong>.</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Now, I want you to pay attention carefully as I'm not going to repeat twice."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, the thing is we thought wrong and we didn't read those copies because we pictured they were or next week."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You may create an app that doesn't communicate well with servers, databases or with its elements leaving it vulnerable to risks."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What is the software architecture? "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The  <strong>software architecture</strong> is the blueprint of the system. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We can say the software architecture embodies all the elements that make a program work, such elements include, processes and data that are related to one another and joined inside the software architecture.</br></br>  Such \u201cblueprint\u201d defines what designs, security, modifiability and performance a piece of software will have  as the engineers who design software create it foreseeing how long it will last and how it is expected to be modified."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "from scratch "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "from the beginning "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(idiom)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Today we'll build an app from scratch to communicate with a remote server."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "picture"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to imagine "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, the thing is we thought wrong and we didn't read those copies because we pictured they were for next week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_wo