eek.<br/>\n<strong>Teacher</strong>: I see, you have to read better next time. Anyway, software architecture can be compared as a depiction of a system that helps  the understanding of how a program works. Let's imagine it is like the blueprint of a program."}, {"time": "59000", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Janet</strong>: Teacher, is it the same as the architectural style?<br/>\n<strong>Teacher</strong>: Let's say that is a subset of it, in other words, an architectural pattern or style is the principle that frameworks an app, by that I mean something like the language the software is going to work with, but not the language of the interface but the one it is going to use to fully communicate within its elements. Therefore, that makes it the most important thing to bear in mind when building an app. <br/>\n<strong>Jeremy</strong>: Why?<br/>\n<strong>Teacher</strong>: Well, let's imagine you create an app without keeping in mind the nature of the architecture, you may create an app that doesn't communicate well with servers, databases or with its elements leaving it vulnerable to risks."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le01ob07re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}